WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:04.160
We know--everyone's finishing out October
with a Stranger Things binge.

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:08.140
But once those final credits roll, how will
you fill that Upside-Down-shaped hole in your

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:09.140
heart?

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:10.380
With more TV, of course!

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:13.900
November is bringing plenty of new movies
and shows to get excited about.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:19.280
Here's everything coming to Netflix in November
2017, starting with the Netflix originals.

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:21.450
Alias Grace: Season 1

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:25.810
Hulu may have snagged The Handmaid's Tale,
but Netflix is fighting back with Alias Grace,

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:28.920
another drama series based on the works of
author Margaret Atwood.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:32.920
Grace is the semi-biographical tale of Grace
Marks, a girl who was convicted of murdering

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:34.800
two people in 1843.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:38.890
The Netflix adaptation stars Sarah Gadon as
the title character and will be released as

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:41.579
a six-part miniseries on November 3rd.

00:00:41.579 --> 00:00:44.499
The Big Family Cooking Showdown: Season 1

00:00:44.499 --> 00:00:48.589
Get ready for a mouth-watering good time with
this unscripted cooking face-off.

00:00:48.589 --> 00:00:52.700
Each episode of The Big Family Cooking Showdown
sees two families go head to head to prepare

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:54.930
the best dish in a series of challenges.

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:59.679
Netflix got distribution rights for this popular
BBC Two cooking show, which originally aired

00:00:59.679 --> 00:01:02.190
in the UK in August 2017.

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:05.199
Stream all of Season 1 on November 3rd.

00:01:05.199 --> 00:01:07.790
Fate/Apocrypha: Part 1

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:12.320
Based on the series of light novels of the
same name, Fate/Apocrypha is an all-new anime

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:16.250
series that follows two warring clans, the
Red Faction and the Black Faction, at the

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:18.720
outbreak of an epic magical war.

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:23.660
Netflix and A-1 Pictures originally aired
the series exclusively in Japan in July 2017,

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:26.420
and they're bringing the dueling mages stateside
on November 7th.

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:31.230
If you're an anime fan, this is one new series
you can't miss.

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:32.740
The Killer

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:36.870
Netflix is extending their international acquisitions
this month with The Killer, a Brazilian crime

00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:40.300
thriller that looks just as intense as its
name would suggest.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:44.890
The story centers on a man named Shaggy who's
on a one-gun mission to track down a notorious

00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:45.890
outlaw.

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:49.200
Netflix hasn't released many details about
this film, but The Killer looks like the Portuguese

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:51.450
spaghetti Western we've all been waiting for.

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:52.960
And we didn't even know it!

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:55.420
Check it out when it hits Netflix on November
10th.

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:58.030
Blazing Transfer Students: Season 1

00:01:58.030 --> 00:02:02.700
If Fate/Apocrypha doesn't sate your anime
appetite, tune in to Season 1 of Blazing Transfer

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:03.700
Students.

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:08.130
While it's not anime--it's a live-action sequel
to the manga of the same name--Blazing Transfer

00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:12.930
Students promises to offer up plenty of anime
style, with a premise so ridiculous we won't

00:02:12.930 --> 00:02:17.710
be able to not watch it: seven boys, all named
Kakeru, get transferred to a new school at

00:02:17.710 --> 00:02:19.829
the same time on a secret mission.

00:02:19.829 --> 00:02:23.459
That's either the worst or the best thing
we've ever heard, and we'll find out for sure

00:02:23.459 --> 00:02:25.930
when the series hits Netflix on November 10th.

00:02:25.930 --> 00:02:28.359
Lady Dynamite: Season 2

00:02:28.359 --> 00:02:32.310
There's always something unexpected in each
episode of Netflix's hit comedy Lady Dynamite,

00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:35.129
and fans can now look forward to a brand new
season.

00:02:35.129 --> 00:02:39.879
Maria Bamford returns as, well, herself to
headline eight new episodes alongside cast

00:02:39.879 --> 00:02:41.489
regular Fred Melamed.

00:02:41.489 --> 00:02:45.450
Both Bamford and Netflix have remained tight-lipped
about what the new season will entail, but

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:49.659
if it's anything like Season 1, we can expect
plenty of Bamford's signature humor.

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:52.680
"I do feel better now that I'm off my meds.

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:54.020
I feel SUPER-charged.

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:56.840
Tune in on November 10th.

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:59.760
DeRay Davis: How To Act Black

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:03.791
Stand-up comedian DeRay Davis lands on Netflix
this November with How to Act Black, a new

00:03:03.791 --> 00:03:07.010
comedy special pulled straight from Davis'
stand-up routines.

00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:10.870
According to Netflix, the special will dive
into life and show business from Davis' point

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:15.749
of view, promising a knock-out series of punchlines
and anecdotes than any comedy fan is sure

00:03:15.749 --> 00:03:16.749
to love.

00:03:16.749 --> 00:03:18.260
Take a look on November 14th.

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:20.379
The Punisher: Season 1

00:03:20.379 --> 00:03:24.439
From the minute he was introduced in Season
2 of Daredevil, fans have been eagerly awaiting

00:03:24.439 --> 00:03:28.670
Frank Castle's solo Netflix outing, and the
wait is finally over.

00:03:28.670 --> 00:03:33.430
Jon Bernthal returns as the skull-shirted
anti-hero on November 17th.

00:03:33.430 --> 00:03:37.180
Season 1 of The Punisher will be comprised
of 13 episodes, and Daredevil's Deborah Ann

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:42.049
Woll co-stars, although there's no hint whether
Daredevil himself will make an appearance--or

00:03:42.049 --> 00:03:44.329
any of the other Defenders, for that matter.

00:03:44.329 --> 00:03:46.659
Jim &amp; Andy: The Great Beyond

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:51.450
In 1999's Man on the Moon, Jim Carrey turned
in a powerful performance as comedian Andy

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:52.450
Kaufman.

00:03:52.450 --> 00:03:56.819
And as the documentary Jim &amp; Andy: The Great
Beyond reveals, Carrey went to insane lengths

00:03:56.819 --> 00:03:57.819
for the role.

00:03:57.819 --> 00:03:59.459
Literally, psychotic lengths.

00:03:59.459 --> 00:04:02.930
The documentary is composed mainly of behind
the scenes footage from the set of Man on

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:03.930
the Moon.

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:08.010
In character every step of the way, Carrey
would torment the director, provoke his co-stars,

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:11.029
and, basically, "Kaufman" the hell out of
the entire production.

00:04:11.029 --> 00:04:15.699
"Universal didn't want the footage we took
behind the scenes to surface so people wouldn't

00:04:15.699 --> 00:04:17.670
think I was an ---hole."

00:04:17.670 --> 00:04:21.670
Even off the set, Carrey enmeshed himself
in Kaufman, once spending two hours on the

00:04:21.670 --> 00:04:25.910
phone with director Ron Howard to talk about
their upcoming film How the Grinch Stole Christmas…

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:27.730
in character as Andy Kaufman.

00:04:27.730 --> 00:04:31.600
It may have worked wonders for Man on the
Moon, but at the same time, it probably explains

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:34.230
just as much about the mess that was Grinch.

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:38.550
You can see the craziness for yourself when
Jim and Andy debuts November 17.

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:40.510
Longmire: Season 6

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:45.410
Saddle up, because Netflix's critically acclaimed
crime drama Longmire is galloping into its

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:48.160
sixth and final season on November 17th.

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:51.690
If we can believe the trailer, this looks
like the end of the road for series protagonist

00:04:51.690 --> 00:04:56.000
Walt Longmire, who's ready to turn in his
badge and give up his life as a lawman.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:05:00.230
Netflix grabbed this modern-day Western when
A&amp;E pulled the plug after three seasons, making

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:03.750
this Longmire's third season under the Netflix
umbrella.

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:05.190
Mudbound

00:05:05.190 --> 00:05:09.370
This Netflix original centers on two soldiers
at the end of World War II who return home

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:14.260
to rural Mississippi, only to find that, in
many ways, their struggles are only just beginning.

00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:18.880
Mudbound premiered at the Sundance Film Festival
in 2017 to critical acclaim, and Netflix picked

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:20.500
it up for distribution.

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:24.100
Sitting tight with an exceptional percent
rating on Rotten Tomatoes, Mudbound definitely

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:26.260
looks like a film worth waiting for.

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:28.310
Check it out on November 17th.

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:30.940
Brian Regan: Nunchucks and Flamethrowers

00:05:30.940 --> 00:05:34.900
With his sarcastic delivery and laid back
comedic style, Brian Regan has been making

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:39.440
audiences laugh for decades now, and he's
back with a new stand-up special coming exclusively

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:40.490
to Netflix.

00:05:40.490 --> 00:05:44.810
Nunchucks and Flamethrowers promises all new
jokes and more of Regan's on-point commentary

00:05:44.810 --> 00:05:46.150
on everyday life.

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:48.280
Check it out on November 21st.

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:50.210
Saving Capitalism

00:05:50.210 --> 00:05:55.520
This movie began life as a Kickstarter campaign
that ultimately raised nearly $300,000 for

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:56.680
the film's production.

00:05:56.680 --> 00:06:00.680
The documentary follows Robert Reich as he
travels the nation to speak to Americans about

00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:04.530
the state of the country and how people with
different political views can find a common

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:05.530
ground.

00:06:05.530 --> 00:06:08.890
Saving Capitalism should offer an interesting
glimpse into the political climate of the

00:06:08.890 --> 00:06:09.890
US.

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:12.630
Look for it on Netflix on November 21st.

00:06:12.630 --> 00:06:13.920
Godless

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:15.560
Are Westerns making their big comeback?

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:21.020
It sure seems like it, and Netflix's upcoming
Godless is the latest outlaw joining the gang.

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:25.550
Starring Jeff Daniels, Godless tells the story
of Frank Griffin, a bandit hellbent on getting

00:06:25.550 --> 00:06:27.360
revenge against his ex-partner.

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:31.580
The six-part miniseries was created by Scott
Frank, who penned Logan, with Steven Soderbergh

00:06:31.580 --> 00:06:33.640
serving as executive producer.

00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:37.640
Get set for all the slick six-shooter action
on November 22nd.

00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:40.000
She's Gotta Have It: Season 1

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:45.020
Spike Lee's 1986 romantic comedy She's Gotta
Have It wasn't a smash hit by any means, but

00:06:45.020 --> 00:06:50.310
it brought in over $7 million on a $175,000
budget, so you could definitely call it a

00:06:50.310 --> 00:06:51.530
financial success.

00:06:51.530 --> 00:06:55.060
And apparently the honchos at Netflix thought
it wouldn't be a terrible idea to capitalize

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:59.090
on that by turning it into a series...even
if it happened 21 years later.

00:06:59.090 --> 00:07:03.360
The show will follow the same premise as the
film: one woman has three lovers, but hesitates

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:04.950
to settle down with any of them.

00:07:04.950 --> 00:07:07.950
Will it capture the same magic as Lee's original
film?

00:07:07.950 --> 00:07:12.920
We'll all have the chance to find out when
Season 1 premieres on November 23rd.

00:07:12.920 --> 00:07:14.810
Cuba and the Cameraman

00:07:14.810 --> 00:07:19.640
After making waves at the Venice International
Film Festival, Jon Alpert's Cuba and the Cameraman

00:07:19.640 --> 00:07:22.360
is set to come out on Netflix on November
24th.

00:07:22.360 --> 00:07:27.110
The documentary chronicles four decades of
revolution, war, and Communism in Cuba under

00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:28.740
the rule of Fidel Castro.

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:34.370
It's not light viewing, but Cuba and the Cameraman
should go on everyone's list of must-see documentaries.

00:07:34.370 --> 00:07:36.670
Frontier: Season 2

00:07:36.670 --> 00:07:40.930
Jason Momoa's gritty period drama is getting
a return with Season 2, launching viewers

00:07:40.930 --> 00:07:43.650
back into the blood-soaked action and frontier
justice.

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:48.091
Created by Rob and Peter Blackie, Frontier
follows Momoa's character Declan Harp and

00:07:48.091 --> 00:07:50.730
his fight against fur traders in Eastern Canada.

00:07:50.730 --> 00:07:53.870
Critics have given the show mixed reviews,
with some praising the action and the set

00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:57.270
pieces and others deriding Frontier's inconsistent
pacing.

00:07:57.270 --> 00:08:01.620
However, if you're looking for something action-packed
to watch while you kick back and relax, you

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:04.770
can catch Frontier Season 2 on November 24th.

00:08:04.770 --> 00:08:06.980
Trailer Park Boys: Out of the Park: USA

00:08:06.980 --> 00:08:11.760
In the first installment of the Trailer Park
Boys' semi-spinoff show Out of the Park, Bubbles,

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:14.810
Julian, and Ricky went to Europe to spread
their shenanigans abroad.

00:08:14.810 --> 00:08:17.060
In the second season, they're heading to the
States.

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:20.889
Some fans felt Out of the Park just wasn't
as good as the show, so fingers crossed the

00:08:20.889 --> 00:08:23.360
second season will bring back that old trailer
park magic.

00:08:23.360 --> 00:08:27.300
"It's Samsquanch, Ricky, and there's one right
outside my f---ing door, right now, he's trying

00:08:27.460 --> 00:08:28.520
to get in my shed."

00:08:29.380 --> 00:08:30.160
"Holy s---, Bubbles, I see him.

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:32.680
Don't scare him, he's f---ing worth a lot
of money."

00:08:32.680 --> 00:08:35.960
Look for Out of the Park: USA on November
24.

00:08:35.960 --> 00:08:37.400
Glitch: Season 2

00:08:37.400 --> 00:08:41.180
There have been several different series about
people mysteriously coming back to life in

00:08:41.180 --> 00:08:42.290
recent years.

00:08:42.290 --> 00:08:47.110
From the French Les Revenants to the American
remake, The Returned, and ABC's unrelated

00:08:47.110 --> 00:08:51.310
Resurrection, this idea somehow became the
most remade trope in recent memory.

00:08:51.310 --> 00:08:55.560
And the Australian telling of the story, Glitch,
is built on the same bones: citizens of a

00:08:55.560 --> 00:08:59.050
small town have to come to grips with the
fact that their loved ones are returning from

00:08:59.050 --> 00:09:00.050
the grave.

00:09:00.050 --> 00:09:03.180
But while the American series fell a little
flat, Glitch was much better received and

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:06.280
went on to win several Australian television
awards.

00:09:06.280 --> 00:09:11.200
Netflix came in to co-produce Season 2, which
airs internationally November 28th.

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:13.200
Good Morning Call: Season 2

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:17.300
Based on a manga of the same name, Good Morning
Call is a romantic comedy series about a girl

00:09:17.300 --> 00:09:20.520
who accidentally becomes roommates with the
hottest boy in school.

00:09:20.520 --> 00:09:25.310
Japanese shenanigans ensue, leading to plenty
of ridiculous situations and a few unexpected

00:09:25.310 --> 00:09:26.310
friendships.

00:09:26.310 --> 00:09:30.320
Season 2 is set to land on Netflix on November
28th, so keep your eyes peeled.

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:31.540
That covers all the Netflix originals.

00:09:31.540 --> 00:09:36.590
Now let's take a look at some of the new movies
Netflix is adding to its lineup in November.

00:09:36.590 --> 00:09:37.860
New movies

00:09:37.860 --> 00:09:41.290
To start with, Netflix is adding a handful
of new action movies this month.

00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:46.130
On the 1st, look for Chappie, a sci-fi action
comedy from District 9's Neil Blomkamp, as

00:09:46.130 --> 00:09:47.160
well as Men in Black.

00:09:47.160 --> 00:09:49.730
"Now that's what I'm talking about."

00:09:49.730 --> 00:09:53.560
November 1st is also seeing the addition of
some classic comedies like the original Scary

00:09:53.560 --> 00:09:55.540
Movie and The Whole Nine Yards.

00:09:55.540 --> 00:09:59.820
For a more serious watch, be sure to check
out brand new documentaries like 2016's It's

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:04.630
Not Yet Dark, an inspiring story about Irish
filmmaker Simon Fitzmaurice, who set out to

00:10:04.630 --> 00:10:09.690
direct a film after he was diagnosed with
neurodegenerative ALS at the age of 34.

00:10:09.690 --> 00:10:11.130
Look for it November 2.

00:10:11.130 --> 00:10:15.880
Other documentaries to watch for this month
include 2017's Williams, a supercharged glimpse

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:20.260
into the founder of the Williams Formula 1
team, and Long Time Running, a music-driven

00:10:20.260 --> 00:10:23.180
glimpse into Canadian rock band The Tragically
Hip.

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:27.730
Netflix's drama lineup is similarly getting
better in November, with 42, Field of Dreams,

00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:31.610
Michael Clayton, and The Pursuit of Happyness
all arriving on the first of the month.

00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:35.260
Those are some hard-hitting films, but don't
worry: Netflix is adding plenty of films for

00:10:35.260 --> 00:10:40.260
family time, too, with Casper and Charlotte's
Web hitting the service on November 1st, Scooby-Doo

00:10:40.260 --> 00:10:44.310
2: Monsters Unleashed on November 13, and
The Boss Baby on November 22nd.

00:10:44.310 --> 00:10:49.190
Then, once the kids are in bed, keep the post-Halloween
chills going with Silent Hill and Oculus on

00:10:49.190 --> 00:10:52.960
November 1st and 2017's Darkness Rising on
the 27th.

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:56.240
But horror shouldn't be too serious, so you
can also look forward to the campy scares

00:10:56.240 --> 00:10:59.810
of 2010's Piranha 3D on November 20.

00:10:59.810 --> 00:11:01.040
New television

00:11:01.040 --> 00:11:04.680
If the first of the month comes and you've
finished binging on Stranger Things already,

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:05.680
don't freak out.

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:07.820
There are plenty of other shows to grab your
undivided attention.

00:11:07.820 --> 00:11:12.860
In addition to The Punisher, Netflix is bringing
on Season 1 of Stranger, a South Korean mystery

00:11:12.860 --> 00:11:16.320
thriller about a police prosecutor on the
hunt for a serial killer.

00:11:16.320 --> 00:11:20.180
The series garnered rave reviews in its home
country, and you can experience all the twists

00:11:20.180 --> 00:11:21.910
and turns on November 1st.

00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:27.420
Also, get ready for police-on-convict action,
COPS style, with Under Arrest: Season 7 dropping

00:11:27.420 --> 00:11:31.190
on the first of the month and Lockup: State
Prisons arriving on the 15th.

00:11:31.190 --> 00:11:35.360
Finally, settle in for the third season of
Broadchurch on November 27th, the critically

00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:39.690
acclaimed British drama that was nominated
for seven BAFTA awards in its first season,

00:11:39.690 --> 00:11:42.980
and which Entertainment Weekly went so far
as to call "a bona fide national obsession."

00:11:42.980 --> 00:11:46.880
"Now that's impressive."

00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:47.880
Thanks for watching!

00:11:47.880 --> 00:11:50.279
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:11:50.279 --> 00:11:52.470
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

